<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to March 8.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to March 8.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry SugarCommittee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June)</p>
<p>sugar crop to March 1 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week March 2-March 8</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,800,566 tns	208,890 tns    11.60 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,867,634 tns	214,451 tns    11.48 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,703,967 tns	182,452 tns    10.71 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to March 8</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    21,941,300 tns    2,339,643 tns    10.66 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    21,270,338 tns    2,226,836 tns    10.47 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    20,091,487 tns    2,081,655 tns    10.36 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 60 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 59 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 59 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
</text>
